## Seasonal Nail Colors for Medium Skin: From Sun-Kissed Summer to Deep Autumn

Medium skin reads differently across seasons, not because the skin changes dramatically, but because light changes, and so does the wardrobe around it. A nail colour that feels proportionate in August can feel slightly off in November, and it is worth having a loose seasonal framework rather than discovering that problem at the salon.

**Spring:** Warm peach nudes, light corals with shimmer, and warm dusty rose. The goal is freshness without going so pale the colour evaporates. A peachy-buff creme in spring reads clean and modern; a flat beige reads simply beige.

**Summer:** Full coral season. Warm poppy red. Golden bronze metallic. Deep peach. Any shade that benefits from the additional warmth and depth that a summer tan brings. Avoid light pastels, they need fair skin to look their best.

**Autumn:** This is when medium skin earns its most dramatic options. Dusty mauve, warm burgundy, burnt sienna, deep berry, earthy terracotta. The seasonal warmth in the palette matches the warmth in your complexion and the results are some of the most flattering nail moments of the year. <a href='https://us.manucurist.com/blogs/journal/best-nail-polish-colors-for-medium-skin' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>Manucurist's medium skin nail edit</a> positions autumn as the high season for medium skin in nail colour, and the range of options confirms it.

**Winter:** The season medium skin navigates most carefully. Without a tan, cool-toned shades are at their most risky. Stick to warm nudes, deep burgundy, warm metallics, and earthy jewel tones, forest green with warm undertones, deep plum with cassis warmth. Avoid anything icy. If you are wearing almond-shaped nails this season, <a href='https://mirelleinspo.com/blog/almond-nail-colors-skin-tone' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>our guide to almond nail colours for every skin tone</a> explores exactly how shape interacts with shade choice on medium complexions.

