## The Framework, Not Just the List

Generic nail advice gives you a colour and tells you to try it. Good nail advice gives you the logic so you can evaluate any shade you encounter, at the salon, at the beauty counter, in a TikTok scroll, and know immediately whether it is for you.

For medium skin, that logic is consistent: lean warm, choose depth over sheerness in most finishes, avoid cool-pink and blue-based formulas, and let the season inform your saturation level. Warm coral is the constant. The right nude is warm-beige or peachy-buff, never sheer-pink. Gold outperforms silver every time. And autumn is the season your skin was made for in nail terms, every rich, warm, dusty shade the palette holds will find its best expression against a medium or caramel complexion.

Your skin has warmth built in already. The nail colour that works does not fight that, it answers it.
